{{!-- META {"path":"svg-animation","title":"SVG animation","description":"Animate the parts of an inline SVG with attributes: stroke drawing, wipes, staggered scenes, travel along a path and shape morphing. Click any drawing on this page to replay it.","parent":"showcase","order":11,"data":{"icon":"pen-nib","preset":"ribbons"}} --}}
{{> page-hero parent=page.parent}}

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div data-sw-animation="fade-up">
      <p class="ws-index ws-ink">01 · A logo, assembled</p>
      <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="v1_title">The Sitewright mark, drawn.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="v1_lead">Three effects on one timeline: the stroke draws, then the two blocks wipe in, each with its own delay. Settings on the root SVG drive the whole drawing: it replays when it comes back into view, replays on a click, and repeats every five seconds.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid cursor-pointer place-items-center rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 py-16">
<!--demo:mark-->
<svg viewBox="0 0 96 96" class="h-48 w-48" fill="none" role="img" aria-label="Sitewright" data-sw-svg-trigger="view" data-sw-svg-replay="true" data-sw-svg-click="true" data-sw-svg-loop="5000">
  <path data-sw-svg="draw" data-sw-duration="1100" data-sw-easing="ease-in-out" d="M30 18 V72 H78" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
  <rect data-sw-svg="reveal-right" data-sw-delay="950" data-sw-duration="500" x="40" y="52" width="26" height="14" rx="3" class="text-accent" fill="currentColor" />
  <rect data-sw-svg="reveal-right" data-sw-delay="1200" data-sw-duration="500" x="40" y="35" width="26" height="14" rx="3" class="text-secondary" fill="currentColor" />
</svg>
<!--/demo-->
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-6">
<!--code:mark file="svg · the mark"-->
  </div>
</section>

<section class="border-y border-base-content/10 bg-base-200/50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
      <p class="ws-index ws-ink">02 · Draw</p>
      <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="v2_title">Lines that draw themselves.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="v2_lead"><code class="font-code text-base">draw</code> animates a stroke from nothing to complete; the element needs a stroke and no fill. <code class="font-code text-base">data-sw-svg-fill="true"</code> fades the fill in after the line is done, the usual move for line-art icons. Put <code class="font-code text-base">draw</code> on a group and every shape inside it draws.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="grid cursor-pointer place-items-center rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 py-14">
<!--demo:draw-->
<svg viewBox="0 0 240 120" class="h-32 w-auto ws-ink" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" data-sw-svg-replay="true" data-sw-svg-click="true">
  <path data-sw-svg="draw" data-sw-duration="1600" data-sw-easing="ease-in-out" d="M12 84 C 40 24 72 24 96 60 C 120 96 152 96 176 60 C 196 30 220 30 228 54" />
</svg>
<!--/demo-->
      </div>
      <div class="grid cursor-pointer place-items-center rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 py-14">
<!--demo:fill-->
<svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" class="h-32 w-auto text-accent" data-sw-svg-replay="true" data-sw-svg-click="true">
  <path data-sw-svg="draw" data-sw-svg-fill="true" data-sw-duration="1400" d="M60 10 L73 44 L110 46 L81 69 L91 105 L60 85 L29 105 L39 69 L10 46 L47 44 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" />
</svg>
<!--/demo-->
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="min-w-0">
<!--code:draw file="svg · draw"-->
      </div>
      <div class="min-w-0">
<!--code:fill file="svg · draw, then fill"-->
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
    <p class="ws-index ws-ink">03 · Scenes</p>
    <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="v3_title">One after another.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="v3_lead">Wrap animated shapes in a <code class="font-code text-base">data-sw-svg-scene</code> and set <code class="font-code text-base">data-sw-svg-stagger</code>; they play in document order as the scene enters the view. These bars rise 110 ms apart.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="grid cursor-pointer place-items-center rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 py-14">
<!--demo:scene-->
<svg viewBox="0 0 320 120" class="h-32 w-auto" data-sw-svg-scene data-sw-svg-stagger="110" data-sw-svg-click="true" data-sw-svg-replay="true">
  <rect data-sw-svg="fade-up" data-sw-duration="600" x="10" y="70" width="44" height="40" rx="8" class="text-primary" fill="currentColor" />
  <rect data-sw-svg="fade-up" data-sw-duration="600" x="72" y="50" width="44" height="60" rx="8" class="text-primary" fill="currentColor" />
  <rect data-sw-svg="fade-up" data-sw-duration="600" x="134" y="34" width="44" height="76" rx="8" class="text-secondary" fill="currentColor" />
  <rect data-sw-svg="fade-up" data-sw-duration="600" x="196" y="20" width="44" height="90" rx="8" class="text-secondary" fill="currentColor" />
  <rect data-sw-svg="fade-up" data-sw-duration="600" x="258" y="8" width="44" height="102" rx="8" class="text-accent" fill="currentColor" />
</svg>
<!--/demo-->
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0">
<!--code:scene file="svg · staggered scene"-->
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="border-y border-base-content/10 bg-base-200/50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
      <p class="ws-index ws-ink">04 · Wipes and entrances</p>
      <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="v4_title">A clean edge, or a familiar entrance.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="v4_lead">The reveal effects uncover a shape in place with a clip-path: right, left, down, up, or an iris from the centre. The entrance effects you know from whole elements work on single shapes too, and scale effects grow from a named corner or edge.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-6">
<!--demo:effects-->
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="cursor-pointer rounded-2xl bg-base-100 p-6 text-primary" data-sw-svg-click="true" data-sw-svg-replay="true" aria-label="reveal-right" role="img"><rect data-sw-svg="reveal-right" data-sw-duration="800" x="10" y="10" width="80" height="80" rx="14" fill="currentColor" /></svg>
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="cursor-pointer rounded-2xl bg-base-100 p-6 text-secondary" data-sw-svg-click="true" data-sw-svg-replay="true" aria-label="reveal-up" role="img"><rect data-sw-svg="reveal-up" data-sw-duration="800" x="10" y="10" width="80" height="80" rx="14" fill="currentColor" /></svg>
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="cursor-pointer rounded-2xl bg-base-100 p-6 text-accent" data-sw-svg-click="true" data-sw-svg-replay="true" aria-label="reveal-iris" role="img"><circle data-sw-svg="reveal-iris" data-sw-duration="900" cx="50" cy="50" r="42" fill="currentColor" /></svg>
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="cursor-pointer rounded-2xl bg-base-100 p-6 text-primary" data-sw-svg-click="true" data-sw-svg-replay="true" aria-label="zoom-in" role="img"><circle data-sw-svg="zoom-in" data-sw-duration="700" data-sw-easing="back" cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="currentColor" /></svg>
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="cursor-pointer rounded-2xl bg-base-100 p-6 text-secondary" data-sw-svg-click="true" data-sw-svg-replay="true" aria-label="flip-x" role="img"><rect data-sw-svg="flip-x" data-sw-duration="800" x="14" y="14" width="72" height="72" rx="10" fill="currentColor" /></svg>
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="cursor-pointer rounded-2xl bg-base-100 p-6 text-accent" data-sw-svg-click="true" data-sw-svg-replay="true" aria-label="scale-bl" role="img"><rect data-sw-svg="scale-bl" data-sw-duration="700" data-sw-easing="bounce" x="14" y="14" width="72" height="72" rx="10" fill="currentColor" /></svg>
<!--/demo-->
    </div>
    <ul class="mt-4 grid list-none grid-cols-2 gap-4 p-0 text-center font-code text-xs text-base-content/60 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-6">
      <li>reveal-right</li><li>reveal-up</li><li>reveal-iris</li><li>zoom-in · back</li><li>flip-x</li><li>scale-bl · bounce</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="mt-6">
<!--code:effects file="svg · wipes and entrances"-->
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
    <p class="ws-index ws-ink">05 · Travel and morph</p>
    <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="v5_title">Along a path, into a new shape.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="v5_lead"><code class="font-code text-base">along-path</code> sends a shape along <code class="font-code text-base">data-sw-svg-path</code>, turned to face its direction. <code class="font-code text-base">morph</code> tweens a path from its own outline to the one in <code class="font-code text-base">data-sw-svg-to</code>; it reads cleanest when the two paths have a similar structure.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="grid cursor-pointer place-items-center rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 py-14">
<!--demo:path-->
<svg viewBox="0 0 240 120" class="h-32 w-auto" data-sw-svg-replay="true" data-sw-svg-click="true">
  <path d="M16 96 Q 120 -8 224 96" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 6" class="text-base-content/30" />
  <circle data-sw-svg="along-path" data-sw-svg-path="M16 96 Q 120 -8 224 96" data-sw-duration="1800" data-sw-easing="ease-in-out" cx="0" cy="0" r="9" class="text-accent" fill="currentColor" />
</svg>
<!--/demo-->
    </div>
    <div class="grid cursor-pointer place-items-center rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 py-14">
<!--demo:morph-->
<svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" class="h-32 w-auto ws-ink" data-sw-svg-replay="true" data-sw-svg-click="true">
  <path class="sw-svg-shown" data-sw-svg="morph" data-sw-svg-to="M60 8 L74 44 L112 44 L82 68 L94 106 L60 82 L26 106 L38 68 L8 44 L46 44 Z" data-sw-duration="1200" data-sw-easing="ease-in-out" fill="currentColor" d="M28 20 H92 A12 12 0 0 1 104 32 V88 A12 12 0 0 1 92 100 H28 A12 12 0 0 1 16 88 V32 A12 12 0 0 1 28 20 Z" />
</svg>
<!--/demo-->
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="min-w-0">
<!--code:path file="svg · along a path"-->
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0">
<!--code:morph file="svg · morph"-->
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="border-t border-base-content/10">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-6" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
        {{sw-icon "eye" "h-6 w-6 ws-ink"}}
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-heading text-lg font-bold">Never hidden for good</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">Without JavaScript, and for visitors who prefer reduced motion, every shape shows its finished state: the drawn line, the morph's starting shape.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-6" data-sw-animation="fade-up" data-sw-delay="80">
        {{sw-icon "timer" "h-6 w-6 ws-ink"}}
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-heading text-lg font-bold">The same timing words</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">Duration, delay, easing and once are the attributes the entrance animations use, plus the springy back, bounce and elastic easings.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-6" data-sw-animation="fade-up" data-sw-delay="160">
        {{sw-icon "pencil-ruler" "h-6 w-6 ws-ink"}}
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-heading text-lg font-bold">A builder in the editor</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">The editor's Library has an SVG animation builder for composing these without writing the attributes by hand.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

